/-!
# Normal refinement and noncentral two-chief accounting

Finite normal filtrations with central or homogeneous binary strata admit
actual chief refinements. Their noncentral two-chief count is the sum of the
supplied multiplicities, and every counted factor carries the specified
conjugation action through its literal quotient coordinates. Repeated coarse
terms and zero multiplicities are allowed.

The precise absence of two-chief factors in the terminal quotient permits
extension to a complete series. Equivariant Jordan–Hölder proves independence
of that series, and every actual noncentral two-chief interval has the same
specified action. The source filtration and its coordinates remain inputs.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*, G.2.5(8),
printed pp.335–336.
-/
